    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d913">

                <pb facs="0938" n="850" xml:id="pg850"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Finch to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Montevideo,
                                Uruguay</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 740.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a communication from
                    United States Consul Hopley, of Montevideo, dated March 12, 1904, relating to
                    the commercial, financial, and industrial condition in and about this capital
                    created by the pending revolution.</p>
                <p>In this connection I will add that the Government continues to assert its belief
                    that the insurrection will soon be suppressed and on its own terms,
                    unconditional surrender. The revolutionary leaders say they will not disband
                    their forces until the Government meets them on a peace basis which at least
                    will stipulate for full pardon and satisfactory assurances of a free ballot and
                    an honest count.</p>
                <p>Respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Finch.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d913-a1.xml" xpointer="d913-a1"/>
            </div>
